{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790970331,"nonce":"rHyAP6QVfNFn1HzEP3dmvCJc0aw=","title":"An imported view never gets its instance-id parameter","message":"`cn_playground_compiles` fails:\n\n    Lowering error: Analysis(\"'forms$FormWidgets$view' takes 0 arguments\n    but is called with 1 in '__blinc_with_3$view'\")\n\n`inject_user_view_instance_id_params` walks one `TypedProgram`'s\ndeclarations and inserts `__instance_id__` ahead of every `view` method\nit finds. `parse_to_typed_ast` runs per file, so each module gets the\npass. A `with` block's synthesized `__blinc_with_N$view` then calls the\ncomponent with the id.\n\nFor a component reaching the entry module through an ES6 import, the\ndefinition that the call resolves against has no such parameter, so\narity disagrees and lowering refuses.\n\nThis surfaced only once blinc_dsl_core compiled again: the crate had not\nbuilt against its zyntax pin, so the test could never run. It is not a\nregression from that fix.\n\nReproduce: `cargo test -p blinc_cn_dsl --test cn_playground`.\n\nSits on the boundary between the multi-module import work and the\nFSM-as-fiber work, and wants a decision about where the injection\nbelongs: per module before import resolution, or once over the linked\nprogram.\n\nCI no longer runs the DSL crates' tests, so this does not gate the\nbuild.","files":null}]}